From 46f1e9bfc93c0d4d8c9754c5ef9d20967585e358 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:29:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] fix(kubevirt): refuse vm_create over an existing
 VirtualMachine

vm_create renders a VirtualMachine and force-applies it. Given the name
of a VM that already exists, the apply replaced its run strategy (a
running VM became Halted), disks, volumes and memory, kept its uid, and
the tool answered "VirtualMachine created successfully". A POST of the
same object is refused with 409 AlreadyExists.

The tool's annotations (destructive, idempotent) and its RBAC metadata
(patch only) suggest the upsert itself may be deliberate at catalog
level; nothing suggests that silently rewriting an existing VM under a
"created" message is. vm_create now reads the VirtualMachine first and,
if it exists, returns an error that names it with its uid and run
strategy and points to vm_lifecycle or resources_create_or_update for
changes. A read error other than NotFound is returned as such. The tool
declares the extra get verb in its RBAC metadata.

The check and the apply are two requests, so a VM created by someone
else in between can still be applied over; closing that window needs a
create (POST) instead of an apply, which changes the tool's declared
verbs and is left for review.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4b00ba93d1277b1ace9317c09ae93e9eeabe5d47)
